Z||000000||Lewis||02-26-2000||12:28 AM||||I was wondering if a electric trunk will open if the nuetral switch is not working..I have a buick also and the trunk will only open if the car is in part or nuetral..so if the nuetral switch on my fiero is not working will the trunk not work either..just wondering if anyone might know...i can not get into the engine compartment because my key lock on the trunk is broke and my dang car will not start...only if I jumpt the selinoid and I just replaced it today...||||reg||9
Z||000001||terryk||02-26-2000||12:56 AM||||It is a seperate switch. So it depends on what you mean by "not working". The swtich controls a relay that controls the solenoid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-26-2000||01:15 PM||||The fiero deck release is neutral interlocked. It is also fused on the dome light curcuit.<P>pull the switch off the dash and jump it. (2 terminals close together on left. The 2 far apart are the light bulb.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||02-27-2000||03:51 AM||||Lewis,<P>Yes, the P/N switch (or the starter solenoid wiring) can keep the trunk release from working. See how to bypass it in your other "It won't start..." post.<P>David.||||reg||1
